# Dev server port

Port 3000 belongs to the person running this repo. Anything you start must not listen on it.

- Do not run `npm run dev`, `next dev`, `next start`, or the same commands with `-p 3000` / `--port 3000`.
- Do not stop, kill, or restart a dev server you did not start in this conversation.
- `npm test` and `npx vitest` do not bind a port. Run them as usual.
- HTTP checks (smoke scripts, `curl`, fetch) may call `http://localhost:3000` only when a server is already running there. Do not start one to make the check possible.
- Two `next dev` processes in this repo share `.next` and break each other even on different ports. Do not start `next dev` while one is already running.
- If a task truly needs its own server, ask first and use another port (for example `3100`). Never take 3000.

```text
# do not run
npm run dev
npx next dev -p 3000

# fine
npx vitest run
# request the server the developer already started
curl http://localhost:3000/login
```
